{
  "category": "Mysterious Pokémon",
  "entries": [
    {
      "text": "Its central core glows with the seven colors of the rainbow. Some people value the core as a gem.",
      "version": "red"
    },
    {
      "text": "Its central core glows with the seven colors of the rainbow. Some people value the core as a gem.",
      "version": "blue"
    },
    {
      "text": "The center section is named the core. People think it is communicating when it glows in 7 colors.",
      "version": "yellow"
    },
    {
      "text": "The center section of its body is called the core. It glows in a different color each time it is seen.",
      "version": "gold"
    },
    {
      "text": "Regardless of the environment it lives in, its body grows to form a symmetrical geometric shape.",
      "version": "silver"
    },
    {
      "text": "It is said that it uses the seven- colored core of its body to send electric waves into outer space.",
      "version": "crystal"
    },
    {
      "text": "STARMIE’s center section - the core - glows brightly in seven colors. Because of its luminous nature, this POKéMON has been given the nickname “the gem of the sea.”",
      "version": "ruby"
    },
    {
      "text": "STARMIE swims through water by spinning its star-shaped body as if it were a propeller on a ship. The core at the center of this POKéMON’s body glows in seven colors.",
      "version": "sapphire"
    },
    {
      "text": "People in ancient times imagined that STARMIE were transformed from the reflections of stars that twinkled on gentle waves at night.",
      "version": "emerald"
    },
    {
      "text": "This POKéMON has a geometric body. Because of its body, the locals suspect that it is an alien creature.",
      "version": "firered"
    },
    {
      "text": "Its central core glows with the seven colors of the rainbow. Some people value the core as a gem.",
      "version": "leafgreen"
    },
    {
      "text": "At the center of its body is a red core, which sends mysterious radio signals into the night sky.",
      "version": "diamond"
    },
    {
      "text": "At the center of its body is a red core, which sends mysterious radio signals into the night sky.",
      "version": "pearl"
    },
    {
      "text": "At the center of its body is a red core, which sends mysterious radio signals into the night sky.",
      "version": "platinum"
    },
    {
      "text": "The middle section of its body is called the core. It glows in a different color each time it is seen.",
      "version": "heartgold"
    },
    {
      "text": "Regardless of the environment it lives in, its body grows to form a symmetrical geometric shape.",
      "version": "soulsilver"
    },
    {
      "text": "At the center of its body is a red core, which sends mysterious radio signals into the night sky.",
      "version": "black"
    },
    {
      "text": "At the center of its body is a red core, which sends mysterious radio signals into the night sky.",
      "version": "white"
    },
    {
      "text": "Its core shines in many colors and sends radio signals into space to communicate with something.",
      "version": "black-2"
    },
    {
      "text": "Its core shines in many colors and sends radio signals into space to communicate with something.",
      "version": "white-2"
    },
    {
      "text": "Its central core glows with the seven colors of the rainbow. Some people value the core as a gem.",
      "version": "x"
    },
    {
      "text": "At the center of its body is a red core, which sends mysterious radio signals into the night sky.",
      "version": "y"
    },
    {
      "text": "Starmie’s center section—the core—glows brightly in seven colors. Because of its luminous nature, this Pokémon has been given the nickname “the gem of the sea.”",
      "version": "omega-ruby"
    },
    {
      "text": "Starmie swims through water by spinning its star-shaped body as if it were a propeller on a ship. The core at the center of this Pokémon’s body glows in seven colors.",
      "version": "alpha-sapphire"
    },
    {
      "text": "Its shining core is thought to receive and transmit enigmatic signals. It has been known to cause headaches in those who approach it.",
      "version": "sun"
    },
    {
      "text": "Its unusual body shape, reminiscent of abstract art, led local people to spread rumors that this Pokémon may be an invader from outer space.",
      "version": "moon"
    },
    {
      "text": "Its sparkling core is called “the gem of the sea.” This core can be made into high-priced accessories that are traded in secret.",
      "version": "ultra-sun"
    },
    {
      "text": "It rotates its geometrically shaped body to swim through the water. It always seems to be sending out mysterious radio waves.",
      "version": "ultra-moon"
    },
    {
      "text": "The center section is named the core. People think it is communicating when it glows in seven colors.",
      "version": "lets-go-pikachu"
    },
    {
      "text": "The center section is named the core. People think it is communicating when it glows in seven colors.",
      "version": "lets-go-eevee"
    },
    {
      "text": "This Pokémon has an organ known as its core. The organ glows in seven colors when Starmie is unleashing its potent psychic powers.",
      "version": "sword"
    },
    {
      "text": "Starmie swims by spinning its body at high speed. As this Pokémon cruises through the ocean, it absorbs tiny plankton.",
      "version": "shield"
    }
  ],
